Subject: Fuse the counted loop's increment and latch test

What this does
  Fuse the counted loop's increment and latch test.

Why we need it
  A rotated counted loop ends in `inc r ; branch_lt r, bound.

What it adds
  New opcode `ROP_inc_branch_lt` (wide and `_s` narrow): the encoder checks the increment is in place (destination and source the same physical register) and the latch reads it, then a pass fuses the pair with the drop/remap machinery `regvm_fuse_self_branch` uses; the int fast path increments, compares and branches, the taken arm carries the back-edge interrupt poll, and anything else tail-calls a slow half that performs the two operations in order.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  Yes. Regenerated register blobs are in `9999`. The monolith configuration is repaired on the way: the capture macro resolves to `sf->regvm_ip` without the record, and `regvm_light_seal` is a no-op when the record path is off.
